From c31d091239193c4d54bfa5a29cedb22bedbf9f3e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pctablet505 <pctablet505@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 23:59:56 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] [Frontend] Return an API error when a chat template
 rejects the request

`chat_template_kwargs={"reasoning_effort": "ultra"}` reached the client as the
model template's own prose with `param: null`, and dumped a full traceback into
the server log, because `safe_apply_chat_template` wraps every failure --
including the template's deliberate `raise_exception` -- in a bare
`ValueError(str(exc))` and logs it with `logger.exception`.

Detect the exact `jinja2.exceptions.TemplateError` that `raise_exception`
raises (subclasses such as `TemplateSyntaxError` and `UndefinedError` mean the
template itself is broken, so they keep their existing handling), and raise a
`ChatTemplateApplicationError` instead: a `VLLMValidationError` so the response
carries `param="chat_template_kwargs"` and names the offending keys, and still
a `ValueError` so existing handlers are unaffected. The status code stays 400.

The template's message already names the values that model accepts, so it is
forwarded verbatim rather than restated against a list that would drift.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
